The other day in wizard mode, I tried to polymorph into something 
nasty and kill a shopkeeper.  So I polmorphed into a baluchitherium
(I know, far from the nastiest critter, because they can't use weapons
or wear armor, but I figured 2 Claw 5d4's were pretty good).  Here's 
what happened:


Really attack Ossipewsk?
You hit Ossipewsk.  You hit Ossipewsk.

[Note: He did not get angry.  He did not hit me back.  So I tried
 it again.]

Really attack Ossipewsk?
You hit Ossipewsk.  You hit Ossipewsk.

[Note again: He's still not angry.  I wait a turn.  Nothing happens.
 I tried attacking him again.]

Really attack Ossipewsk? [yn] y
You hit Ossipewsk.  Ossipewsk is killed!
Welcome to experience level 6.



I tried this later with different monsters in different shops.  It
seems that whenever you attack the shopkeeper with your bare hands,
and hit him, he doesn't get angry.  If you miss him, he does get 
angry.  If you use a weapon, he does get angry.  This only works if
you polymorph into something else, not if you are human and hit him
with your bare hands.

I haven't look at the source yet to see why this happens.  Any ideas?
